  "notes": [
    "HarfBuzz is the REFERENCE implementation, not a sibling port. go-text/typesetting was rejected as the oracle: it would break gomod_test.go's wantModuleGraph, and it descends from the same benoitkugler/textlayout lineage textshape's README credits, so its agreement is weaker evidence than it looks.",
    "textshape's own harfbuzz-tests/ corpus was rejected too: a vendor's test corpus is curated by the vendor and selected to pass. This oracle runs HarfBuzz against FOLIO8's corpus.",
    "Precedent: Story 1.1 used qpdf --check as an external oracle specifically to avoid a module dependency, and AD-25 permits provenance by 'a one-time offline reference run, hand-checked — never a runtime dependency'.",
    "Cluster values here are RUNE indices, matching textshape. See the Thai name row, whose clusters are 0,0,2,3,3,5,5 — byte offsets over seven three-byte runes would be multiples of 3."
  ]
}
